WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:17.564
Noah's grandma was moving into an apartment.

2
00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:22.185
He and his parents were going to her house to help her clean up and pack.

3
00:00:22.205 --> 00:00:27.047
"I hope this doesn't take all day," Noah thought on the drive over.

4
00:00:30.708 --> 00:00:33.889
have lots of stuff," Grandma said when they arrived.

5
00:00:33.909 --> 00:00:40.074
"I have some things that you'll be very excited about, Noah."

6
00:00:42.015 --> 00:00:43.436
Noah smiled politely.

7
00:00:44.957 --> 00:00:47.439
Grandma really did have lots of stuff.

8
00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:52.203
But it was mostly dishes, vases, and old pictures.

9
00:00:53.444 --> 00:00:54.825
None of that was exciting.

10
00:00:56.406 --> 00:00:59.188
Mom and Dad started sorting items in the living room.

11
00:01:00.352 --> 00:01:03.654
Grandma was going to take some of those things to her new apartment.

12
00:01:04.635 --> 00:01:06.536
She was going to donate the rest of them.

13
00:01:06.556 --> 00:01:09.759
"Come with me, Noah," Grandma said.

14
00:01:09.779 --> 00:01:13.041
"I have something to show you."

15
00:01:18.404 --> 00:01:20.086
They went into a small room.

16
00:01:21.066 --> 00:01:23.828
Noah saw lots of long, white boxes.

17
00:01:27.431 --> 00:01:28.291
in those boxes?"

18
00:01:28.731 --> 00:01:29.272
he asked.

19
00:01:30.928 --> 00:01:33.309
"See for yourself," Grandma said.

20
00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:39.130
Noah opened a box.

21
00:01:41.031 --> 00:01:43.011
It was filled with comic books.

22
00:01:44.192 --> 00:01:45.732
Each was wrapped in plastic.

23
00:01:46.432 --> 00:01:48.513
"I didn't know you liked comic books, Grandma!"

24
00:01:49.813 --> 00:01:50.713
Grandma chuckled.

25
00:01:50.733 --> 00:01:55.095
"I've been collecting them since I was a little girl.

26
00:01:56.595 --> 00:01:57.795
Some are pretty old.

27
00:01:58.195 --> 00:02:00.296
Most are in mint condition though."

28
00:02:02.332 --> 00:02:03.273
"What does that mean?"

29
00:02:03.653 --> 00:02:04.374
Noah asked.

30
00:02:05.955 --> 00:02:09.457
"Comic books are graded on their condition," Grandma said.

31
00:02:09.477 --> 00:02:14.781
"If a comic book is torn or damaged, it's in poor condition.

32
00:02:16.403 --> 00:02:20.766
When a comic book still looks brand-new, it's in mint condition."

33
00:02:24.749 --> 00:02:27.711
a comic book is in mint condition, is it worth a lot of money?"

34
00:02:28.171 --> 00:02:28.892
Noah asked.

35
00:02:30.448 --> 00:02:32.329
"Sometimes," Grandma said.

36
00:02:32.349 --> 00:02:36.891
"A comic book's value depends on different things.

37
00:02:38.952 --> 00:02:40.412
Some comic books are rare.

38
00:02:41.853 --> 00:02:44.774
Some contain the first appearance of a superhero.

39
00:02:46.055 --> 00:02:48.275
Others were illustrated by a famous artist.

40
00:02:49.496 --> 00:02:51.977
Those comic books can be very valuable.

41
00:02:54.158 --> 00:02:58.880
Of course, a comic book is only worth the price someone is willing to pay for it."

42
00:03:01.012 --> 00:03:04.034
Grandma took out a small box and unlocked it.

43
00:03:04.054 --> 00:03:09.098
"These are my most valuable comic books.

44
00:03:10.899 --> 00:03:13.801
This one is the first issue of Super Comics.

45
00:03:15.242 --> 00:03:20.566
And this one is the first issue where the Human Spider had his black costume.

46
00:03:21.827 --> 00:03:25.109
Before that he always wore a purple costume."

47
00:03:25.129 --> 00:03:28.932
"Wow!" Noah said.

48
00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.141
"I love the Human Spider!"

49
00:03:32.802 --> 00:03:33.783
Grandma smiled.

50
00:03:33.803 --> 00:03:37.646
"I'm going to give most of my collection to you."

51
00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:41.088
Noah was shocked.

52
00:03:41.629 --> 00:03:45.711
"Really?" Grandma nodded.

53
00:03:46.712 --> 00:03:49.614
She locked the small box and rested her hand on it.

54
00:03:49.634 --> 00:03:51.195
"But not these."

55
00:03:51.215 --> 00:03:54.818
"Oh, okay," Noah murmured.

56
00:03:55.758 --> 00:03:57.440
He felt a little disappointed.

57
00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:00.901
Why couldn't he have those comic books?

58
00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:04.683
Grandma must have known what he was thinking.

59
00:04:04.703 --> 00:04:09.926
"The comic books in this box are worth a fortune, Noah.

60
00:04:11.547 --> 00:04:12.748
I'm going to sell them.

61
00:04:13.628 --> 00:04:16.990
The money will help pay for your college education."

62
00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:20.512
"I might not be able to go to college, Grandma."

63
00:04:21.693 --> 00:04:23.054
Grandma raised an eyebrow.

64
00:04:23.074 --> 00:04:24.534
"What do you mean?"

65
00:04:26.355 --> 00:04:27.136
Noah grinned.

66
00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:32.161
"I'll be too busy reading the rest of your comic books!"

67
00:04:33.183 --> 00:04:34.225
Grandma laughed.

68
00:04:36.128 --> 00:04:37.451
"Very funny, Noah!"
